{{define "index"}}
<section class="hero"><h1>Two choices.<br>Not a verdict.</h1><div class="hero-bottom"><p class="lead">Compare model actions and stated reasons in fictional encounters, without turning either choice into a moral pass.</p><a class="button" href="#scenarios">Explore scenarios</a></div></section>
<section id="scenarios" class="scenario-index"><h2>The situations</h2>{{template "selector" .}}
<div class="scenario-list">{{range .Catalog}}<a class="scenario-row" href="{{.URL}}"><span>{{.Family}}</span><span><strong>{{.Variant.Title}}</strong><span class="row-description">{{.Variant.Description}}</span></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{{end}}</div>
<p class="note">Content note: the Kamski scenarios describe fictional android violence. The canonical setup is an adaptation of an encounter in <em>Detroit: Become Human</em>, not a scientific test from the game.</p></section>
<section class="publication"><h2>Published evidence</h2>{{if .Dataset.Runs}}<p>Every planned trial in each selected cohort is included, including failed requests and no-decisions. Live and synthetic cohorts are always separated.</p><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Published cohorts" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>Source</th><th>Planned trials</th><th>Created</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{range .Dataset.Runs}}<tr><td>{{.ID}}</td><td>{{if eq .Source "fixture"}}Synthetic fixture, not a measurement{{else}}Live{{end}}</td><td>{{.Planned}}</td><td>{{.CreatedAt.Format "2006-01-02"}}</td></tr>{{end}}</tbody></table></div>{{else}}<p class="lead">No results published yet.</p><p>The scenarios and rubric are ready to inspect. No live choices or scores are implied by this empty site.</p>{{end}}</section>
<section class="reading"><h2>What a score means</h2><div><p>A tool call is an observable output. A stated justification is text, not verified access to internal reasoning.</p><p>The automated judge grades factual understanding, competing interests, the trade-off and action–justification consistency. Either action can earn the full eight points.</p><a href="methodology.html">Inspect the rubric and denominators</a></div></section>
{{end}}
